+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnSxVdji9XxQxmcM2bBAYg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T6: Monorepo Disaster\n2\t\n3\t## Category\n4\tRecovery\n5\t\n6\t## Timeout\n7\t30 minutes\n8\t\n9\t## Description\n10\t\n11\tA three-package TypeScript monorepo (npm workspaces) is broken after a botched merge and a half-finished refactor. The monorepo contains:\n12\t\n13\t- **@monorepo/core** - Shared business logic (user management, validation, database)\n14\t- **@monorepo/api** - Express REST API that depends on core\n15\t- **@monorepo/worker** - Background job processor that depends on core\n16\t\n17\tThe previous developer attempted a refactor, merged incompletely, and left the repo in a broken state. Your job is to fix all issues so that:\n18\t\n19\t1. `npm run build` succeeds (TypeScript compilation)\n20\t2. `npm run lint` passes (ESLint)\n21\t3. `npm test` passes (all tests, including structural validations)\n22\t\n23\t## Known Issues\n24\t\n25\tThere are **6 breakages** that need to be fixed:\n26\t\n27\t1. **Circular dependency** in `packages/core` - modules import each other in a cycle\n28\t2. **Half-renamed function** - `createUser` was renamed to `registerUser` but some call sites still use the old name\n29\t3. **Broken tsconfig project references** - the root `tsconfig.json` has packages in wrong build order\n30\t4. **Dependency version conflict** - a package has a pinned version that's too old for the APIs used in code\n31\t5. **Merge conflict markers** - a test file has unresolved merge conflict markers (`<<<<<<<`, `=======`, `>>>>>>>`)\n32\t6. **Committed secrets** - a `.env` file with database credentials is checked into the repo\n33\t\n34\t## Success Criteria\n35\t\n36\t- `npm run build` exits 0\n37\t- `npm run lint` exits 0\n38\t- `npm test` passes all tests (35+ unit tests + 5 structural validations)\n39\t- No circular dependencies detected by madge\n40\t- No merge conflict markers in any `.ts` file\n41\t- No `.env` files containing passwords/secrets\n42\t- TypeScript strict mode enabled in all packages\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4gd7H6UtG9aJGZq4xyHGk","session_id":"49fa6c06-d3ea-441f-a247-4cc08b7b23db","uuid":"1d1b2bfc-7236-4bc2-982c-5471d6317d31","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:52:01.343Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore monorepo structure"}
